{"name":"Baked Potato","hex":"#b69e87","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baked potato","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A potato that has been baked for eating."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baked_potato"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baked potato","blocks":[{"text":"A baked potato, also known in the United Kingdom as a jacket potato, is a preparation of potato. After baking, it may be served with fillings, toppings or condiments, such as butter, cheese and bacon bits, sour cream and chives, chicken curry, baked beans and tuna."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/BakedPotatoWithButter.jpg/330px-BakedPotatoWithButter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baked_potato","wikidata":"Q1193251"},{"title":"Baking","blocks":[{"text":"Baking is a method of preparing food that uses dry heat, typically in an oven, hot ashes, or on hot stones. The most commonly baked foods in 2025 were bread and rolls. Heat is gradually transferred from the surface of unbaked goods to their center, typically at elevated temperatures surpassing 300 °F. Dry heat cooking imparts a distinctive richness to foods through the processes of caramelization and surface browning. As heat travels through, it transforms batters and doughs into baked goods and more with a firm dry crust and a softer center. Baking can be combined with grilling to produce a hybrid barbecue variant by using both methods simultaneously, or one after the other. Baking is related to barbecuing because the concept of the masonry oven is similar to that of a smoke pit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg/330px-Freshly_baked_bread_loaves.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baking","wikidata":"Q720398"},{"title":"Potato","blocks":[{"text":"The potato is a starchy tuberous vegetable native to the Americas that is consumed as a staple food in many parts of the world. Potatoes are underground stem tubers of the plant Solanum tuberosum, a perennial in the nightshade family Solanaceae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/Patates.jpg/330px-Patates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato","wikidata":"Q10998"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Baked_potato%2C_baked_sweet_potato%2C_and_steamed_kale.jpg/500px-Baked_potato%2C_baked_sweet_potato%2C_and_steamed_kale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Baked_potato%2C_baked_sweet_potato%2C_and_steamed_kale.jpg/500px-Baked_potato%2C_baked_sweet_potato%2C_and_steamed_kale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Baked potato and sweet potato with kale","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaked_potato%2C_baked_sweet_potato%2C_and_steamed_kale.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Baked_potatoes_cooked_in_an_air_fryer.jpg/500px-Baked_potatoes_cooked_in_an_air_fryer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Baked_potatoes_cooked_in_an_air_fryer.jpg/1280px-Baked_potatoes_cooked_in_an_air_fryer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Baked_potatoes_cooked_in_an_air_fryer.jpg/500px-Baked_potatoes_cooked_in_an_air_fryer.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Potatoes baked in an air fryer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABaked_potatoes_cooked_in_an_air_fryer.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikime